    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=4$.\n\nTake logarithms to base $2$ and factor the quadratic in $\\log_2 x$.",
      "worked": "The original domain is $x>0$. Take logarithms to base $2$ of both positive sides.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\log_2 x-4)\\log_2 x&=-4\\\\(\\log_2 x)^2-4\\log_2 x+4&=0\\\\(\\log_2 x-2)^2&=0\\\\\\log_2 x&=2\\\\x&=4\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x=4$, the original left-hand side is $4^{-2}=\\frac1{16}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
